   224	The exact polynomial identity is
   225	
   226	`p(k)=p0(k+delta)-p0(delta)`.
   227	
   228	Using oddness of p0, this gives `eta_i=theta_i-epsilon_i*theta_0` for **both** F and G types, with exactly the dispersions stated in §1. This explicitly accounts for the shifted background.
   229	
   230	Introduce a formal nonzero charge variable u. In the proved auxiliary family of §4 with indices `0,1,...,N`, set
   231	
   232	```text
   233	(a_0,b_0)=(u,0),
   234	(a_i,b_i)=(u*A_i,0)                                  for F type,
   235	(a_i,b_i)=(0,u^(-1)*A_i*lambda*k_i/(lambda*k_i-1))    for G type.
   236	```
