by (17).
   In summary, the 1SS is given by (19,21) where the parameters are constrained by (22).
For KdV the dispersion relation is q 3 = p.


3.2     The two-soliton solution
The 2SS is built from two 1SS’s, and one important principle is that for integrable systems
one must be able to combine any pair of 1SS’s built on top of the same vacuum. Thus if
we have two 1SS’s, F1 = 1 + eη1 and F2 = 1 + eη2 , we should be able to combine them into
a form F = 1 + f1 + f2 , where f1 = eη1 + eη1 . Gauge invariance suggest that we should
try the combination
