Definition: A set of equations written in the Hirota bilinear form is Hirota inte-
grable, if one can combine any number N of one-soliton solutions into an NSS, and the
combination is a finite polynomial in the eη ’s involved.

In all cases known so far, Hirota integrability has turned out to be equivalent to more
conventional definitions of integrability.


4     Searching for integrable evolution equations.
Since the existence of a 3SS is very restrictive, one can use it as a method for searching
for new integrable equations. All search methods depend on some initial assumptions
about the structure. In this case we assume that the nonlinear PDE can be put into a
bilinear form of type (16), but no assumptions are made for example on the number of
independent variables.




